title the tree answers what a file cannot
prompt Keaton said kg cross-file -- build the reachability pass that tells a pub proof function from a pub API function.
think Started by measuring the discriminator rather than assuming it. A bare-name grep was too coarse: check_refusals appears in seven files because each caravan ring defines its own. The qualified call form .name( reads zero for the three proof functions and eighteen for crop.
obs Then found the trap in my own test: scale_bilinear is real API with no caller anywhere in the tree, so a no-external-caller rule alone would have binned it proof. Added a second condition -- the function returns void -- and both err toward CONTRACT when unsure, since a contract read as proof hides a gap while a proof read as contract only inflates one.
think Wrote the control legs before trusting the number, and they caught two things. The void detection required the brace at end of line, so it read real caravan code and refused a one-line fixture; loosened it so both read the same.
obs The second was mine and worth naming: flush() processes the file that just ENDED, and I passed FILENAME to the cross-file check, which by then already holds the NEXT file. Every lookup was asking about the wrong file. The control found it; the tree-wide number would have looked plausible either way.
obs And one control leg was stale rather than wrong -- its fixture gave crop a void return where the real crop returns a pixmap. Made the fixture match what it protects instead of loosening the rule to pass it.
obs caravan 217 to 171, pond 39 to 24, tree gap 453 to 400. Verified nothing wrongly left: the eight rooms swept this season read 737 of 737 exactly as before.
obs lattice surfaced six real contract asserts in lattice_core.rye once its selftest file stopped hiding them -- matrix index bounds and a shape agreement. Swept, three blocks.
loom cross_file rule=no_qualified_call_elsewhere+returns_void control=24 wall_s=8.4
loom tree pct=97 gap=400 caravan=217->171 pond=39->24 unchanged_rooms=737/737
file tools/fixtures/invariant_coverage_scan.sh the qualified-call pre-pass and the two guards
file tools/fixtures/invariant_coverage_control.sh three legs for the rule, one fixture corrected
file lattice/lattice_core.rye three blocks over six asserts
